# Hermetic build dependency bootstrap

Implement `tools/build/dependencies.py` with CPython 3.14.6 as the declared
bootstrap and install public project dependencies into repository-owned pinned
locations without mutating global packages; validate proprietary or platform
toolchains as explicit external prerequisites instead of silently using
arbitrary host state.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Require CPython 3.14.6 for the supported workflow and emit a clear
  user-facing diagnostic for any other version.
- [ ] Install or verify public dependencies deterministically under
  repository-owned `.dependencies/` and `.cache/` locations without global
  package mutation.
- [ ] Treat Unreal Engine and unavoidable platform SDK or signing material as
  declared external prerequisites whose exact versions are checked rather
  than vendored.
- [ ] Make repeated successful runs idempotent and persist machine-readable
  dependency evidence for later build steps.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency is required beyond the declared repository and
platform prerequisites.

## Evidence

Add implementation, deterministic validation, and supported-host evidence here
as the task advances.
